    "result": "Perfect! All 28 tests pass across all test files. Here's what I fixed:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n**1. Fixed `governance.test.js` failure** - File: `/packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js`\n   - Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n   - The test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export to construct error messages, but it was only available in the default export\n\n**2. Fixed `eval/index.test.js` failure** - File: `/packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js`\n   - Modified `runEvaluations()` to check function arity before passing parameters\n   - `toxicityMetric` only requires outputs (bannedTerms is optional), while other metrics need both outputs and references\n   - By checking `metric.length >= 2`, the function now passes references only to metrics that expect them\n   - This prevents references from being incorrectly used as \"banned terms\" in the toxicity check\n\nThe fixes maintain backward compatibility\u2014all existing public exports continue to work as before, and the test suite now fully passes.",
